-front contribution.\",\n      \"source_reported_band_breadth_km\": 200,\n      \"total_current_width_km\": null,\n      \"secondary_core_width_km\": null,\n      \"nominal_section_longitude_degrees_east\": 1,\n      \"primary_surface_front_station_latitudes_degrees_north\": [\n        -38,\n        -37\n      ],\n      \"secondary_core_latitudes_degrees_north\": [\n        -40,\n        -39\n      ],\n      \"source_approximate_core_offset_south_of_primary_front_km\": 200,\n      \"core_offset_is_width\": false,\n      \"front_or_core_bracket_is_width_edges\": false,\n      \"relative_geostrophic_reference\": {\n        \"potential_density_symbol\": \"sigma_4\",\n        \"value_kg_m3\": 45.87,\n        \"source_reference_depth_range_m\": [\n          3470,\n          3560\n        ],\n        \"reference_is_width_layer\": false\n      },\n      \"field_plot_depth_context_m\": [\n        0,\n        1000\n      ],\n      \"field_plot_context_is_uniform_width_layer\": false,\n      \"transport_context\": {\n        \"source_rounded_southern_band_sv\": 8,\n        \"source_rounded_sac_sv\": 17,\n        \"table2_southern_band_sv\": 8.3,\n        \"table2_at_front_sv\": 8.8,\n        \"table2_north_of_front_sv\": -1.4,\n        \"integration_depth_range_m\": [\n          0,\n          1000\n        ],\n        \"transport_is_width_uncertainty\": false,\n        \"width_derived_from_transport\": false\n      },\n      \"display_title\": \"Historical southern component band\",\n      \"display_aria_label\": \"South Atlantic Current: authors report a200 km wide southern component band at1 E in October1983. The primary front carries additional SAC flow; total SAC width and secondary-core diameter unknown. Relative geostrophic reference sigma4=45.87 kg/m3 at3470-3560 m. Width depth, edges, exact days and error unknown; no annual range.\",\n      \"display_caption\": \"October 1983 / Knorr section k at 1 E. Source-reported southern component band breadth; additional SAC flow crosses the primary front. Total-current width unknown.\",\n      \"display_method_note\": \"200 km describes the southern band, not the entire SAC or the diameter of its secondary core. The similarly sized core offset is distinct. Width-evaluation depth, edge cutoff, paired geographic boundaries and numerical error remain unknown. No annual or seasonal inference.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"remaining_scientific_gates\": [\n    \"Recover paired geographic width edges and explicit boundary criterion.\",\n    \"Recover exact width evaluation depth and occupation days.\",\n    \"Acquire compatible repeated same-component sections before annual or seasonal comparison.\"\n  ]\n}\n","status":"source_reviewed_local_component_not_whole_current_width"},{"current_id":"portugal","document":{"current_id":"portugal","figure_file":"figures/portugal-orca-2009-section-span.svg","figure_sha256":"b36d9ba1bab10f47558528eddef4407b5ec8cdcd3524e28b779a845f019efa88","measurement":{"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"approximate_width_km":116,"boundary_rule":"Published current-band coordinate limits; no independently digitized velocity cutoff or physical edge.","calendar_months":null,"current_id":"portugal","extraction_method":"WGS84 inverse geodesic between previously curated source limits; display rounded to nearest kilometre. No figure digitization.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"ORCA northern section at 37 N, Portugal band between 14.8 and 13.5 W, stations 19-23.","id":"portugal-perez-2009-orca-source-section-span","is_confidence_interval":false,"layer":"Surface and thermocline flow in neutral density layers 1-4 (gamma_n < 27.3800 kg/m3). Fixed depth bounds are not supplied.","measurement_type":"published_coordinate_derived_local_section_span","name":"Portugal Current","observed_period":null,"phase_kind":"campaign_coordinate_derived_section_span","phase_label":"ORCA local section / fall 2009","published_section_context":{"calculation_ellip