stated time, layer and reference, with eastern SIOC identity checked. Keep the 80 E surface-component diagnostic separate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"current_id\": \"south-australian\",\n      \"source_index\": 1,\n      \"source_locator\": \"AppendixB continuation and AppendixC, original p17; parsed dataset/method sections2.1-2.4\",\n      \"finding\": \"The paper uses fixed boxes around shelf-break currents to calculate transport. Those boxes do not provide measured current edges or seasonal width extrema.\",\n      \"control_volume_context\": {\n        \"north_latitude_offset_degrees\": 0.375,\n        \"south_latitude_offset_degrees\": 0.375,\n        \"reference_isobath_m\": 700,\n        \"reference_isobath_is_sampling_depth\": false,\n        \"geographic_scope\": \"Shelf-break control volume west of Portland; not whole southern-Australia system or whole South Australian Current.\",\n        \"offsets_are_physical_current_edges\": false,\n        \"kilometre_width_derived\": false\n      },\n      \"temporal_product_guard\": \"CARS annual mean and the final seven years of climatologically forced MOM01 are separate from the 2012 HYCOM profiles at 100 m and from calendar-year observations.\",\n      \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\n      \"new_width_record_admitted\": false,\n      \"next_required_evidence\": \"Compatible boundaries for a stated time and layer, plus verified current association. Keep the 132 E, 100 m HYCOM component diagnostic separate.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_figures_or_original_pdf_redistributed\": false,\n  \"prepared_for\": \"Current-card and query source context; no numeric gap marked filled.\",\n  \"measurement_coverage_counts_changed\": false\n}\n","status":"source_review_registered_current_width_unresolved"},{"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","document":{"acquisition_sha256":"dc684f969378f2ada64a6174fa23810ade8bbe8db2f86ea77e849384b7d95fae","annual_extrema_eligible":false,