y.v1","seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"source_doi":"10.1029/2022JC019147","source_percentages_are_fit_targets":false,"status":"feasibility_only_not_current_width_admission","whole_current_width_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false},"entity_id":"current:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","id":"diagnostic:current-research:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Indian South Equatorial Countercurrent research evidence","rank_eligible":false,"research_evidence":{"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","diagnostic_id":"diagnostic:current-research:indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent","facts":[{"label":"Pattern-current association","value":"Not independently verified"},{"label":"Current width","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Annual width range","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Source coverage","value":"Two native columns \u00b7 1995\u20132016"}],"figure_alt":"Three statistical loading patterns and monthly coefficients at two native longitudes. Northern support is incomplete; no current width is admitted.","figure_file":"figures/indian-secc-eof-feasibility.svg","figure_sha256":"65cb81417d19c9b4ebb1f6cbd1f0e5a003a67686bc877b9f6c08ace4f803aafb","finding":"Two neighboring OSCAR columns over 1995\u20132016 show similar leading statistical patterns. The southern pattern peaks near 5\u00b0S, with an April maximum in its monthly coefficient climatology. This does not verify a named current or its physical edges.","geometry_role":"research_evidence_no_current_axis_or_physical_width_geometry","kind":"current_research_evidence","label":"Indian South Equatorial Countercurrent","new_width_record_admitted":false,"next_evidence":"Independent flow association and comparable transverse velocity sections before physical-width admission.","notes":["Five northern latitudes fail complete monthly support. Missing observations are not land or zero flow; the northern pattern peaks at the retained data edge.","Latitude bands are paper classification context, not current boundaries. Principal-component coefficients are not local current speeds.","Three latitude windows and both native columns remain separate. Similarity within one product is not independent validation or a confidence interval.","Exact author domain/weighting/code were unavailable; this experiment is not an exact reproduction."],"original_url":"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019147","rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/indian-secc-eof-classification-feasibility.json","source_links":[{"document":"research/indian-secc-eof-classification-feasibility.json","label":"Inspect all fits and comparisons","pointer":""},{"document":"research/source-data/oscar-indian-eof-1995-2016/acquisition.json","label":"Inspect acquisition receipt","pointer":""},{"document":"research/source-data/oscar-indian-eof-1995-2016/preflight.json","label":"Inspect declared calculation","pointer":""}],"source_pointer":"","table":{"caption":"Primary-window variance by native column; statistical patterns, not named-current widths.","headers":["Native longitude","Mode 1","Mode 2","Mode 3"],"rows":[["80.333\u00b0E","51.3%","19.0%","14.0%"],["80.667\u00b0E","51.0%","18.5%","14.6%"]]},"title":"Seasonal patterns: classification evidence","whole_current_width_km":null},"source_file":"research/indian-secc-eof-classification-feasibility.json","source_file_sha256":"1ec87c83802445c8685a091fc1b8d9a7d70755bc203dd3c09e14baafa0e2d144","source_json":"{\n  \"schema\": \"osw.indian-current-eof-classification-feasibility.v1\",\n  \"status\": \"feasibility_only_not_current_width_admission\",\n  \"preflight_sha256\": \"b9c19d3c1abd87bf9b1c03910d383905a07de73ba2a957f597f83ab1224587a9\",\n  \"acquisition_sha256\": \"dc684f969378f2ada64a6174fa23810ade8bbe8db2f86ea77e849384b7d95fae\",\n  \"datasets\": [\n    {\n      \"longitude\": 80.33333333333333,\n      \"source_frames\": 1585,\n      \"excluded_times\": [\n        \"2017-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n      ],\n     