0359f4c3b056a8506795b02a5eb866dabb47385"},"whole_current_width_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false},"entity_id":"current:red-sea-saline-overflow","id":"diagnostic:current-research:red-sea-saline-overflow","label":"Red Sea saline overflow research evidence","rank_eligible":false,"research_evidence":{"additional_figures":[{"alt":"Twelve source-ordered casts on 22\u201323 February 2001, paired layer velocities, hydrography and all fixed southern sensitivities. Primary local span about 5.0 km, deeper-layer half-peak 5.5 km; northern and shallow-layer results unresolved. Physical whole-current width and annual range unknown.","file":"figures/redsox-winter-section3-component-spans.svg","label":"Independent source-declared winter section"},{"alt":"February and August 2001 paired layer components and salinity from twelve repeated station neighborhoods. Winter southern spans are about5.0/5.5km; summer northern candidate3.1km fails the unchanged saline screen and is not a verified width. Southern summer is quality-blocked; northern winter is incomplete. No same-branch width difference or annual range is supported.","file":"figures/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.svg","label":"Two dated surveys: velocity and salinity comparison"}],"additional_tables":[{"caption":"Independent Section 3, 22\u201323 February 2001. Local half-peak section spans; not whole-current widths.","headers":["Layer above bottom","Southern local span","Northern local span"],"rows":[["20\u201360 m","About 5.0 km","Unresolved"],["10\u201350 m","Unresolved","Unresolved"],["40\u201380 m","About 5.5 km","Unresolved"]]},{"caption":"22\u201323 February versus23 August2001, Section3. Different branches are separate; component candidates are not physical widths. All six same-branch dated differences remain unresolved.","headers":["Layer above bottom","Winter south","Summer south","Winter north","Summer north","Same-branch difference"],"rows":[["20\u201360 m","About 5.0 km","Unresolved","Unresolved","About 3.1 km \u00b7 saline screen fails","Unresolved"],["10\u201350 m","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved"],["40\u201380 m","About 5.5 km","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved","Unresolved"]]}],"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","diagnostic_id":"diagnostic:current-research:red-sea-saline-overflow","facts":[{"label":"Earlier northern section span","value":"About 6 km \u00b7 40\u201380 m above bottom"},{"label":"Earlier primary 20\u201360 m result","value":"Unresolved"},{"label":"Whole-current width","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Annual width range","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Independent southern section","value":"About 5.0 km \u00b7 20\u201360 m above bottom"},{"label":"Independent northern section","value":"Unresolved"},{"label":"Summer northern component candidate","value":"About 3.1 km \u00b7 saline screen fails"}],"figure_alt":"Winter and summer layer velocity and salinity. A roughly 6 km secondary-layer local span is distinguished from unknown primary and summer outcomes.","figure_file":"figures/redsox-lower-nc-section-diagnostic.svg","figure_sha256":"f56167fb865d8a8eca58b00cbc8a496a7414097dabcbf2487f56c490d356c8b7","finding":"Winter casts 7, 8 and 9 support a roughly 6 km half-peak southward-component section span in the layer 40\u201380 m above bottom. This local-core follow-up is separate from the unresolved primary calculation at 20\u201360 m. It does not establish a whole-current or flow-normal width. A separate source-declared cross-channel section on 22\u201323 February supports a southern local span of about 5.0 km at 20\u201360 m above bottom and 5.5 km at 40\u201380 m. Its northern branch remains unresolved. The 23 August repeat gives a northern component candidate near 3.1 km, but it fails the unchanged saline-water screen. No same-branch winter\u2013summer width difference is supported.","geometry_role":"research_evidence_no_current_axis_or_physical_width_geometry","kind":"current_research_evidence","label":"Red Sea saline overflow","new_width_record_admitted":false,"next_evidence":"Resolve rejected-component treatment and water-mass/flow association; obtain paired usable boundaries and repeated observations before physical-width or seasonal-range admission.","notes":["The local span covers only 1.67 native station spacings. The core vector is about 15.7\u00b0 from the section normal; no cosine correction or precise physical-boundary claim is made.","The 40% threshold remains unresolved. Finite velocity, boundary and layer scenarios are not combined into a confidence interval.","A conditional value near 7.3 km in the 20\u201360 m layer uses excluded winter cast 10 and does not replace the primary unknown. Summer lacks comparable usable layer/reference support; it is not zero width or proof of an absent current.","Original headers, reviewed metadata and filename-only cast joins remain distinct. The declaration-history note records prior incidental exposure to three cast 10 rows; no fully blinded preregistration is claimed.","The new section preserves all 30 fixed cases: ten southern component spans and twenty unresolved outcomes. The deeper-layer 40% threshold extends to 12.6 km; this is finite scenario sensitivity, not an annual margin or confidence bound. The 10\u201350 m layer lacks complete support. Casts 61/63 remain excluded; cast 74 has no CTD companion. No tidal removal or whole-current width admission.","The summer peak has about 37.41 source psu, below the unchanged 38 psu screen; the \u22120.04 m/s offset also puts it below the speed floor. This does not prove the named outflow is absent. Cast22 remains excluded for unverified bad-upcast treatment. All30 summer cases and all6 same-branch comparisons are retained. Two dates cannot establish an annual range or seasonal climatology; different branches are never combined to fill missing comparisons."],"original_url":"https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/archive/accession/0146147","query_links":[{"label":"Query all dated section measurements","query":{"collection":"current_section_measurements","filters":[{"field":"current_id","op":"eq","value":"red-sea-saline-overflow"}],"limit":100}}],"rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/redsox-lower-nc-dated-section-diagnostic.json","source_links":[{"document":"research/redsox-lower-nc-dated-section-diagnostic.json","label":"Inspect all layers and null scenarios","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-ladcp-source-inventory.json","label":"Inspect direct-current source inventory","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-ctd-companion-inventory.json","label":"Inspect hydrography and filename joins","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-cruise-log-metadata-reconciliation.json","label":"Inspect reviewed source metadata","pointer":""},{"document":"research/source-data/redsox-lower-nc-2001/declaration-history-note.json","label":"Inspect declaration-history qualification","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-winter-section3-component-spans.json","label":"All 30 independent section cases","pointer":"/layers"},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-source-selection.json","label":"Source section selection and original hashes","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-source-selection.json","label":"Declared independent section rules","pointer":"/protocol_file"},{"document":"research/redsox-winter-section3-figure.json","label":"Independent section figure provenance","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","label":"Summer section: all 30 declared cases","pointer":"/summer_layers"},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","label":"Six same-branch dated comparisons","pointer":"/comparisons"},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-surveys.json","label":"Matched source station positions","pointer":"/station_correspondence"},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-source-selection.json","label":"Summer section selection and rules","pointer":""},{"document":"research/redsox-section3-repeat-figure.json","label":"Repeat-survey figure provenance","pointer":""}],"source_pointer":"","table":{"caption":"Two non-synoptic 2001 surveys; outcomes are section diagnostics, not annual current widths.","headers":["Survey","Layer above bottom","Supported local half-peak span"],"rows":[["18 Feb 2001","20\u201360 m","Unresolved"],["18 Feb 2001","10\u201350 m","Unresolved"],["18 Feb 2001","40\u201380 m","About 6 km \u00b7 follow-up"],["24 Aug 2001","20\u201360 m","Unresolved"],["24 Aug 2001","10\u201350 m","Unresolved"],["24 Aug 2001","40\u201380 m","Unresolved"]]},"title":"Observed sections: independent local span estimates","whole_current_width_km":null},"source_file":"research/redsox-lower-nc-dated-section-diagnostic.json","source_file_sha256":"fc247b8090793bdcc62e6073d51522fa21e756759fde4caab6383dba84e0f3c5","source_json":"{\n  \"schema\": \"osw.redsox-matched-lower-NC-feasibility.v1\",\n  \"preflight_sha256\": \"c9aa43ff540a180e606b984400aaa29d20f525e91dfee12b17791ece53c98660\",\n  \"followup_preflight_sha256\": \"cfced47f8fc78bb1fc37b1e6033f499e687afab5239388f104d330a6e0dd410a\",\n  \"implementation_clarifications_sha256\": \"2fbf9636562ee5e22e420e1355220bded6368ab05aee82fe92f9949cc8e8a81b\",\n  \"declaration_history_qualification_file\": \"research/source-data/redsox-lower-nc-2001/declaration-history-note.json\",\n  \"declaration_history_qualification_sha256\": \"23f5f47e82136efe661cb35422b7d2bc7447648048965d1f44a75bb6c6fb9123\",\n  \"calculation_rules_declared_before_layer_and_span_computation\": true,\n  \"fully_blinded_before_any_selected_velocity_exposure\": false,\n  \"source_ladcp_inputs\": {\n    \"research/source-data/ncei-redsox-2001/preflight.json\": \"334a989a2b2f5205d345584f8c471641bac3eea7be4a44ab360cb1881a855b41\",\n    \"research/source-data/ncei-redsox-2001/acquisition.json\": \"f6453064d837cefa689fa274e72c5d5b84bcae85d119910a48f1092d7f11236c\",\n    \"research/source-data/ncei-redsox-2001/documentation.json\": \"12c56f526