56":"a93829b63315edff1aa3ef0bdadfd9e8119c6578ecf7578863e13967f4c0797c","finding":"All twelve months retain 8,784 hourly model fields at 10 m, with complete support at the 191 fixed section positions. This improves seasonal sampling in the offshore Ingoy region; the section is not a verified current axis or a current-width measurement.","geometry_role":"research_evidence_no_current_axis_or_physical_width_geometry","kind":"current_research_evidence","label":"Norwegian Coastal Current","new_width_record_admitted":false,"next_evidence":"Establish flow association and comparable paired physical boundaries before admitting a current width or annual width range.","notes":["Monthly means use all calendar hours, including leap day. Source spacing is 800 m; retained spacing is 3.2 km. Interpolated section positions add no native resolution.","The 24/24/25-hour low-pass convolution attenuates tides and other high-frequency variability. It is not a harmonic tidal solution.","Temporal standard deviations and sample quantiles describe model variability, not confidence intervals or current-width uncertainty. Serial dependence remains.","This is a single model year at one layer, not observations, a climatology or a depth average. The offshore region does not establish coastal extent or physical current edges.","The declaration records prior exposure to twelve isolated snapshots; no fully blinded preregistration is claimed. Modified Norkyst data: MET Norway / Institute of Marine Research, CC BY 4.0.","Calculated readbacks use a declared precision for reproducibility. That precision is not observational uncertainty or an annual range. Original source values, masks and quality flags remain unchanged; the exact record pins the calculation rules."],"original_url":"https://thredds.met.no/thredds/catalog/romshindcast/norkyst_v3/zdepth/catalog.html","rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/source-data/norkyst-ingoy-months-2024/section-diagnostic-year.json","source_links":[{"document":