m/s"},"whole_current_length_km":null,"whole_current_width_km":null,"year":2013},"entity_id":"current:pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","id":"diagnostic:current-research:pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","label":"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent research evidence","rank_eligible":false,"research_evidence":{"additional_figures":[{"alt":"Monthly peak directions and connected eastward-component spans across three native columns. Attention guides are not error bounds, annual ranges or flow-normal widths.","file":"figures/necc-paired-2013-direction-column-context.svg","label":"Direction and native-column context"}],"annual_width_range_km":null,"current_id":"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","diagnostic_id":"diagnostic:current-research:pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent","facts":[{"label":"Paired source support","value":"7,992 vectors \u00b7 3 native columns"},{"label":"Archive sampling","value":"72 timestamps \u00b7 2013"},{"label":"Physical current width","value":"Unknown"},{"label":"Annual width range","value":"Unknown"}],"figure_alt":"Monthly eastward and northward near-surface OSCAR fields at three native longitudes in 2013. Dots are selected component peaks, not a current axis or physical edges.","figure_file":"figures/necc-paired-2013-monthly-vector-sections.svg","figure_label":"Monthly paired components","figure_sha256":"10e7bf099ae583a6a10fa393d8348f19195bad734a67dcba4248271aa254296b","finding":"Both velocity components are retained at 140 W and its two native neighbors. All twelve central monthly means and component spans reproduce the earlier calculation. Nine of 36 selected monthly peaks depart more than 15 degrees from east, reaching about 46 degrees. These are product diagnostics, not physical current widths.","geometry_role":"research_evidence_no_current_axis_or_physical_width_geometry","kind":"current_research_evidence","label":"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent","new_width_record_admitted":false,"next_evidence":"Compatible independent velocity sections, verified named-flow association, source-error assessment and transverse physical edges before current width, annual ranges or mapped width admission.","notes":["This is archived satellite-derived OSCAR 2017.0 near-surface velocity, not direct instrument sections. Nominal depth coordinate 15 m is product context.","Actual source times run from 1 January to 26 December 2013, including four six-day gaps. Equal-sample monthly means are not daily/time-weighted means or a climatology.","Directions are derived from paired monthly-mean vectors, not averaged source-frame headings. No cosine correction turns the component spans into flow-normal widths.","The 15-degree and two-native-cell attention guides are OSW choices, not admission limits or confidence intervals. Three months show larger peak-latitude separation between columns; same-product neighbors are not independent validation or measurement-error bounds.","The 1/3-degree grid does not establish independent effective resolution. Cells outside the selected component, including westward flow, are not assigned to the named NECC.","Target u was viewed before the new declaration. New v and neighboring velocity acquisition followed the declaration commit; no fully blinded or externally timestamped preregistration is claimed.","Calculated readbacks use a declared precision for reproducibility. That precision is not observational uncertainty or an annual range. Original source values, masks and quality flags remain unchanged; the exact record pins the calculation rules."],"original_url":"https://oceanwatch.pifsc.noaa.gov/erddap/info/yearly_336c_0b32_9cd3/index.html","rank_eligible":false,"source_file":"research/pacific-necc-paired-vector-direction-evidence.json","source_links":[{"document":"research/pacific-necc-paired-vector-source-inventory.json","label":"Inspect paired source vectors","pointer":"/samples"},{"document":"research/pacific-necc-paired-vector-direction-evidence.json","label"